SUMMARY:Deadline: Foresight Institute AI Nodes RFP\, Track II: Coordination
  and Accountability
DESCRIPTION:Track II of Foresight Institute's AI for Science & Safety Nodes
  RFP funds ways for increasingly capable AI systems to coordinate with eac
 h other\, the people using them\, and the wider world\, without handing po
 wer to a single model\, lab or government. THREE FOCUS AREAS: (1) Supercol
 laboration and decentralized alignment: coordination and credit-assignment
  protocols\, tooling for massive human-AI collectives\, incentive designs 
 robust to gaming\, mutual monitoring and cross-checking among agents\, sca
 lable verification\, and open coordination protocols built on boundaries a
 s Schelling points for multi-agent coordination. (2) Human Empowerment: ev
 idence\, decision rules and working tools for when human control genuinely
  empowers people versus when AI delegation is preferable\, including a 'wh
 en to defer control' framework and mechanisms to detect and fix hollow ove
 rsight. (3) AI Insurance and Open Governance: building a middle layer betw
 een lab self-governance and government regulation\, such as ways for insur
 ers to judge and price frontier-lab risk\, independent incident reporting 
 and assessment that does not leak lab secrets\, and mechanisms like develo
 per mutuals\, catastrophe bonds or liability for near-misses. Selected pro
 jects receive grant funding\, private local compute\, workspace at the San
  Francisco or Berlin AI Nodes\, travel-paid field-building events and acce
 ss to Foresight's advisors and network\; in-person contributors at the Nod
 es are strongly prioritised. Individuals\, teams\, and nonprofit or for-pr
 ofit organisations worldwide may apply (for-profits must justify their nee
 d for grant funding). Deadline 31 October 2026\, 23:59 PDT.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Foresight Institute\nLocation: Remote (global\; hubs in San Francisco a
 nd Berlin)\nAward: Typically $30\,000 to $100\,000 per grant\, with smalle
 r amounts for the Human Empowerment and AI Insurance & Open Governance foc
 us areas\; plus private local compute and workspace at the San Francisco o
 r Berlin AI Nodes. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\n\nMore: h
 ttps://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-coordination-and-a
 ccountability/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://foresight.org/grants/ai-science-safety-nodes-rfp-coordination-a
 nd-accountability/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
