SUMMARY:Deadline: Intron: Sahara CodeSwitch Africa Challenge
DESCRIPTION:Intron's Sahara CodeSwitch Africa Challenge awards USD 10\,000 
 in cash prizes for real applications built on African voice AI: apps that 
 understand African-language code-switching\, for example when a speaker mo
 ves between English and Swahili\, English and Igbo\, or French and Wolof m
 id-conversation. TRACKS: Health (clinical documentation\, patient intake\,
  maternal health)\; Legal and Public Services (court transcription\, legal
  aid\, citizen services)\; Fintech\, Telco and Customer Experience (voice 
 banking\, KYC\, payments\, support)\; Agriculture and Education (farmer ad
 visory\, tutoring\, classroom learning)\; and Other High-Impact Use Cases 
 (accessibility\, media\, commerce\, culture). REQUIREMENTS: use voice to a
 chieve a downstream task (not just speech-to-text)\, build with the Intron
  Sahara API\, benchmark Sahara against at least three other speech models\
 , target a specific vertical\, and include code-switched audio samples whe
 re possible. WHO IS ELIGIBLE: developers\, researchers\, startups\, studen
 t teams and NGOs across Africa and the diaspora\; solo or teams. DEADLINE:
  registration and final submissions close 15 September 2026\, 11:59pm WAT\
 , so move fast. Winners announced 1 October 2026. TO APPLY: register at in
 tron.io/compete. Free to enter.\n\nOrganisation: Intron\nLocation: Remote\
 ; open to builders across Africa and the diaspora\, solo or in teams (2 to
  5 recommended).\nAward: USD 10\,000 total prize pool in cash prizes acros
 s five tracks. Finalists also get Sahara API credits\, Partner Demo Day ac
 cess\, visibility with sponsors and judges\, and potential pilot or deploy
 ment conversations. Free to enter.\nDuration: Main competition winners ann
 ounced 1 October 2026\n\nMore: https://intron.io/compete?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://intron.io/compete?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\; open to builders across Africa and the diaspora\, solo or
  in teams (2 to 5 recommended).
END:VEVENT
