SUMMARY:Deadline: ARDC: Amateur Radio and Digital Communications Grants (Ja
 nuary 2027 round)
DESCRIPTION:ARDC funds amateur radio\, wireless technology education\, and 
 communications research and development\, including software-defined radio
 \, mesh and packet networking\, and open RF tooling\, which puts it square
 ly at the transmission-art and community-network end of creative tech. WHA
 T YOU GET: grants with no stated minimum or maximum\; the published 2026 p
 ortfolio ranges from USD 1\,285 to USD 258\,000\, so both small education 
 projects and major open-source radio infrastructure are funded. CONDITIONS
 : all funded work must be released openly (GPL\, MIT\, BSD\, CERN OHL or C
 C licenses). ELIGIBILITY: US 501(c)(3) nonprofits\, government agencies\, 
 schools and universities\, and international nonprofits and schools\; indi
 viduals\, artist collectives and radio clubs must apply through a nonprofi
 t fiscal sponsor\, which is routine in the US but adds overhead. APPLICATI
 ON: open now on a quarterly cadence\; the September 2026 round has closed\
 , so the next actionable deadline is 15 January 2027\, with evaluation tak
 ing 60 to 120 days.\n\nOrganisation: Amateur Radio Digital Communications 
 (ARDC)\nLocation: USA-based funder\, worldwide reach. US 501(c)(3) nonprof
 its\, government agencies\, schools and universities\, and international n
 onprofits and schools\; individuals\, collectives and radio clubs apply th
 rough a nonprofit fiscal sponsor.\nAward: No fixed range is stated on the 
 apply page\, but ARDC's published 2026 grant portfolio shows awards from U
 SD 1\,285 up to USD 258\,000 (for example GNU Radio 4 at USD 258\,000). No
  application fee.\nDuration: Quarterly grant cycles (deadlines 15 January\
 , 1 April\, 1 July\, 1 September)\; evaluation takes 60 to 120 days.\n\nMo
 re: https://www.ardc.net/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
